Subject: [PATCH] rendervulkan: require a DRM primary node only for the DRM backend

The device check rejects any GPU without a primary node unless the backend presents through a Vulkan
swapchain. The primary node's dev_t is consumed only by the DRM backend (vulkan_primary_dev_id, read in
DRMBackend.cpp); the Wayland and headless backends hand their buffers to a host or to nobody, and need
only the render node opened just below. A render-only GPU paired with a separate display controller —
Apple AGX under Asahi (Honeykrisp), most ARM SoCs — has no primary node, so the Wayland backend refused
to start there and fell back to SDL.

Gate the requirement on the session-based (DRM) backend.
diff --git a/src/rendervulkan.cpp b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
index 77134f2..4a8042d 100644
--- a/src/rendervulkan.cpp
+++ b/src/rendervulkan.cpp
@@ -480,7 +480,9 @@ bool CVulkanDevice::createDevice()
 		};
 		vk.GetPhysicalDeviceProperties2( physDev(), &props2 );
 
-		if ( !GetBackend()->UsesVulkanSwapchain() && !drmProps.hasPrimary ) {
+		// Only the DRM backend scans out through the primary node (DRMBackend reads vulkan_primary_dev_id);
+		// a nested backend presents through its host, so a render-only GPU is enough.
+		if ( GetBackend()->IsSessionBased() && !drmProps.hasPrimary ) {
 			vk_log.errorf( "physical device has no primary node" );
 			return false;
 		}
